  "overview": "**dotUI** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#e31c5f` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Helvetica Now Text` (32px display down to 16px body), unified by `.5rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nSource: published token package (https://github.com/mehdibha/dotUI), repo https://github.com/mehdibha/dotUI. Inventory: **90** colors, **233** typography steps, and **26** documented components (see repository license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 26 component tokens with documented paddings: `0`, `.25rem`, `1.5rem`, `2px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f5f5f5` cards; separate sibling sections using `#e5e5e5` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 25px 50px -12px oklch(0% 0 0/.25)`) paired with `#e5e5e5` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#e31c5f` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#e31c5f` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.3:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Helvetica Now Text` headings with `Helvetica Now Text` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `.5rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (.5rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f5f5f5` surface shifts and `#e5e5e5` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `.5rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
